# Version bumps require consent

Do **not** change version numbers unless the user explicitly asks (e.g. “bump to 0.3.10”, “cut a release”).

## Do not touch without asking

- `mod.package.props` `<Version>`
- Thunderstore / Hexium dependency version pins (`DrakeMods-DrakeModsLibs-…`, etc.)
- `CHANGELOG.md` version headings that imply a new release number
- Any other package/manifest version fields (`manifest_template.json`, etc.)

## When implementing features/fixes

- Ship code + docs under the **current** version already in the repo.
- You may add bullets under the **existing** top changelog section if it is clearly still unreleased / in progress — do not invent a new `## x.y.z` section.
- If a dependency version pin must change for the build to work, **ask first** and wait.

## Why

The maintainer owns release numbering. Agents that auto-bump fight manual version fixes and create noisy diffs.
